                "Choose where they go: your collection, a new deck or an existing deck, and tap Save.",
                "Browse your cards in Collection and your decks in Decks. Tap a card for its image, price and links.",
                "Back up now and then via More → Settings and backup, or turn on the weekly automatic backup.",
            )),
            Tip("Every screen has a ? at the top right. It opens the chapter for that screen. The whole guide is at the top of More, with a search bar."),
        )),
        Chapter("import", "Importing from the Sheet", "Bring your existing collection over in one go.", listOf(
            Steps(listOf(
                "Open your MTG Collection Sheet in Google Sheets. On a computer: File → Download → Microsoft Excel (.xlsx). In the Google Sheets app: ⋮ → Share and export → Save as → Excel.",
                "In NineGrid go to More → Import (or Collection → + → Import). Tap Choose Sheet in Google Drive and pick your Sheet: Android delivers it as Excel, no download needed. A downloaded file you pick with Choose a file. Exports from Moxfield, Archidekt, ManaBox, Deckbox, Dragon Shield, TCGplayer, Delver Lens and Helvault are recognised automatically; for an unknown format you point out the columns once.",
                "For a file from another app you choose whether it goes to your collection or becomes one deck.",
                "You see what was found: tabs, cards in your collection, decks and history. If the app already has cards, choose Add or Replace everything.",
                "Tap Import. This runs in the background with a notification: you can use or close the app meanwhile. If Scryfall asks for a pause, the app waits and continues by itself. If the phone restarts, the import continues where it was.",
                "When it is done you get a notification. Tap it for the result.",
                "Cards that were not found can be copied as a list and added later via Paste list.",
                "If a number in your file belongs to another card than the name, NineGrid uses the name. Those lines are listed afterwards under Number did not match, so you can correct them in your file.",
            )),
            P("Set tabs and Loose cards go to your collection, the Decks tab is imported per deck with Commander, Deck and Sideboard. Foil, etched, language, quantity and proxy come along. History becomes the chart line. The Overview tab is skipped."),
            Tip("The whole import is one change: undo it in one go via More → Change log."),
            Note("Writing back to your Sheet (syncing) comes later; that needs a Google connection."),
        )),
        Chapter("add", "Adding cards", "Scanning, an existing photo, pasting a list or searching one card.", listOf(
            H("Scanning"),
            Steps(listOf(
                "Tap Scan at the bottom. The camera fills the whole screen; the arrow at the top left takes you back. The first time, the app asks for camera permission.",
                "Tap Set at the top to enter the set code, for example MH1. If all cards are from one set, do this: the set code is the smallest text on the card and this makes recognition much more reliable. The app remembers the set for next time; with a ✓ in front, it is filled in. Mixed page? Leave it empty. Binder and Page are for tracking where cards are; the after each saved page the page number goes up by one (not with 1 card). Undo the save and the page number goes back too.",
                "Choose Page (9 cards) or 1 card with the switch at the bottom. For a page, a small grid of the page appears at the bottom after the photo, with a ✦ in the corner: that is where you set foil. The border of each slot shows how sure the recognition is: green sure, orange doubt, red not found. Tap the grid, then tap a slot in the big grid to make that card foil (gold border and ✦), or tap All foil. For 1 card use the Foil (card) button. Long press a slot to open the review screen. The camera view stays free for focusing. Lay the page flat and hold the phone straight above it so the page fits between the white corners and each cross sits roughly in the middle of a card. The frame is the grid: an empty slot stays empty without shifting the other cards, and shows in grey as Empty slot (not as something to check). Only what is inside the frame counts. Tap the image to focus; the Light button at the bottom right helps in low light; Gallery at the bottom left reads a photo you already had.",
                "Tap the big orange button in the middle. The camera focuses first, then the app reads each card's name at the top and its set and number at the bottom. If the photo is blurry or the page too small, you get a message with Try again or View anyway.",
                "A short flash and vibration show that the photo was taken; it appears as a small picture in the result (tap to see it large). While the app reads and looks up, a ring spins around the button.",
                "You stay in the camera. The result is in colour: ● green found, ● orange to check. When everything is found, tap Save and scan the next page right away. When something needs checking, tap Check (with the count on it). To see how long recognition took, turn on Settings → Scanning → times and tap the small photo.",
                "With AI help on, the AI then reads the orange and red slots. The slot gets an AI label: blinking = busy, filled = read and confirmed by Scryfall, struck through = did not work. Tap the label in the big grid for the reason. Above the result you see \"AI is reading 3 slots…\" while it runs.",
                "Failed? Tap 🗑 on the left of the result: the scan is gone at once, with Restore in the message. With 1 card, 🗑 only discards the last card.",
                "After saving, the message has an Undo button in case you made a mistake.",
            )),
            Tip("Good light without glare works best. Tilt foils slightly until the shine is gone."),
            Note("Foils have a star (★) between set and language at the bottom. If the scanner reads that star, it already sets the card to foil and the slot turns orange: \"★ read: foil?\". Tap the slot in the large grid to confirm it (another tap turns foil off), or check it on the review screen."),
            Note("Cards in other languages (for example MH1 • FR): set and number count, the language is stored with the card and the price is that of the print. Online, the app also checks the printed name; if it does not match, the card is orange. For Japanese, Chinese and Korean the name is not read, so make sure the bottom line is sharp."),
            Note("Photos are only read on your phone and never stored or sent."),
            H("Scanning single cards"),
            Steps(listOf(
                "Choose 1 card at the bottom. The frame takes the shape of one card, and Automatic is on.",
                "Put a card in the frame and hold the phone still. After half a second the app takes the photo itself: the frame blinks green and the phone vibrates.",
                "Put down the next card. The same card again? Take it away briefly and put it back: it counts one more (×2, ×3).",
                "The last three cards are shown at the bottom. Remove a mistake with the cross.",
                "Tap Done to see them all in the review screen and save them.",
            )),
            Tip("The volume buttons are also a shutter button. How long the card must lie still is set in Settings (fast, normal or sure). If no card is seen for two minutes, watching pauses; tap Paused to continue."),
            Tip("The app remembers whether you last used Page or 1 card."),
            H("Without internet"),
            P("Without a connection the app keeps the scan as Waiting for connection, even if you close the app. As soon as you are online again, the cards are looked up automatically."),
            H("Using an existing photo"),
            P("On the scan screen tap the photo button at the bottom left and choose a photo from your gallery. The rest works the same as scanning."),
            H("Pasting a list"),
            P("Via Collection → + → Paste list, More → Paste list, or inside a deck. One card per line:"),
            P("1 Edgar Markov (INR) 328\n4 Murder (M20) 109 *F*\n1 Sol Ring (C21) 263 *E*"),
            Steps(listOf(
                "*F* after a line means foil, *E* means etched.",
                "A line Commander, Deck or Sideboard starts a new section. SB: before a line puts that card in the sideboard.",
                "Without headers, everything after a blank line is sideboard.",
                "Set and number may be missing; the app then searches by name.",
            )),
            Tip("Lists from Moxfield, Archidekt and MTG Arena can usually be pasted as they are."),
            H("Searching one card"),
            P("Tap + in Collection → Search card, type part of the name, pick the card and then the right print."),
        )),
        Chapter("review", "The review screen", "Checking cards before they are saved.", listOf(
            P("After scanning or pasting you see every card with image, set, number and quantity. Cards that were not found are shown in red, with what the scanner did read. A scan always lists all 9 slots; if a slot is really empty, untick it."),
            Steps(listOf(
                "With a scan, a cut-out of your photo is shown on the left next to the card that was found. Tap it to see both large side by side; that way you see right away whether it is the right print.",
                "Not found? Tap the magnifier and search the card yourself. You can see what the scanner read, which helps.",
                "Wrong print? Tap the card → More options → Choose other print.",
                "Change the quantity with − and +. Toggle Foil with the button below.",
                "Under More options: finish (non-foil, foil, etched), language, condition (NM by default) and proxy.",
                "Don't want to save a card? Untick it on the left.",
                "At the top choose where the cards go: Collection, New deck or Existing deck.",
                "Tap Save at the bottom.",
            )),
            H("Binder, page and slot"),
            P("When you choose Collection you can enter a binder and page number. When scanning, each card then gets its slot automatically (1 top left, 9 bottom right). After saving, the page number moves up by one so you can scan the next page right away."),
            Note("Scan a page that is already in the app and you get a warning: Already scanned? You decide whether to add it anyway."),
            H("Commander"),
            P("Making a Commander deck? Tap the Commander button on the card that leads the deck. You can save without one, but the deck check will mention it."),
        )),
        Chapter("collection", "Your collection", "Searching, filtering, the card screen and locations.", listOf(
            Steps(listOf(
                "Search by name at the top. The Filter button (the number = how many are on) lets you choose rarity, colour, card type, foil, Game Changers, Include decks and Also rules text; you can pick several per group, for example Rare and Mythic.",
                "What is on is shown under the search bar; tap the cross to turn it off, or Clear filters. Filters and sorting are remembered. The funnel is filter, the arrows are sort (set, price or name).",
                "No image? A small mark says why: Wi-Fi only, offline, or no image at Scryfall. The card page spells out the reason, with Load anyway when it is only the Wi-Fi setting.",
                "Sort by price or name. Cards are grouped by set.",
            )),
            H("The card screen"),
            P("Tap a card for the card screen: the card large at the top (tap for full screen; a foil shines when you tilt the phone), below it name, type, set and legality per format. On wishlist (or Add to collection) puts it on your list. The Price block shows normal and foil, which friends have it, and links to Scryfall and Cardmarket (or TCGplayer when using dollars)."),
            P("Your copies lists every copy with its location and details:"),
            Steps(listOf(
                "− and + change the quantity.",
                "Move puts (part of) the stack into a deck, or back into your collection with binder, page and slot.",
                "Edit changes finish, language, condition and proxy.",
                "Delete removes the copies from the app.",
            )),
            Note("Proxies are shown in grey and do not count in totals or value."),
            H("Set complete"),
            P("Tap a set in Overview. At the top is a card with how much of the set you own (for example 130 of 254 · 51%), a bar per rarity, what the missing cards cost together, and Completionist. As soon as you scroll, that card collapses to one line; tap it for the details."),
            P("The switch chooses Missing or I have, each with its count. Under Missing the images are dimmed, and on the right are ♡ (to the wishlist, exactly this print) and + (add). Under I have you see per card how many you own, how many foil and where it is. Tap a card for the card screen. With Count variants, borderless, showcase and extended art count too."),
        )),
        Chapter("allcards", "All cards and wishlist", "Searching all Magic cards, keeping a wishlist and setting a price alert.", listOf(
            P("At the top of Collection is a switch: My collection, All cards and Wishlist."),
            H("All cards"),
            Steps(listOf(
                "Choose All cards and type at least 2 letters, or turn on a filter. Online, the app searches half a second after your last letter.",
                "Below the search bar is the source: the offline card database (instant, no internet) or online at Scryfall (per page, Load more at the bottom).",
                "Each card has a label: green In collection ×3 or In deck Edgar. No label = you don't have it. The filter Only what I don't have shows just those. With the Game Changers filter the app searches Scryfall (that needs internet), because the offline database does not know that list.",
                "Tap a card for the card screen with price, legality and prints. There you find Add to collection and On wishlist.",
            )),
            Tip("Your recent searches are below the search bar. With Also rules text the app always searches online: the offline database has no rules text."),
            H("Wishlist"),
            Steps(listOf(
                "Put a card on your wishlist from All cards, the card screen, an almost-combo or an AI buy suggestion, or paste a list via ⋮ → Paste list to wishlist.",
                "Tap a card for the card screen. By default any print is fine. Use the pencil (✎) to edit: an exact print, foil only, and how many you want (in the list: 1 of 4). The Game Changers button at the top shows only the Game Changers on your list. With any print you see the price of the cheapest print (from …); below the name you see the price alert and which friend has it.",
                "Scan or import the card and the app ticks it off by itself, saying so in the message.",
                "The ✓ on the right (Bought) puts the card in your collection in one tap, with the chosen print and quantity.",
            )),
            H("Price alert"),
            P("Under Edit you set a price alert. The target is already the current price minus 10%. The app checks once a day, after the price update. If more cards drop below their target, you get one notification. A card alerts once per drop, and again only after it has been above the target. With any print, the alert looks at the cheapest print."),
        )),
        Chapter("binders", "Binders and page view", "Filtering, sorting and browsing your binders page by page.", listOf(
            Steps(listOf(
                "Filter Collection by Binder (also No binder), together with other filters.",
                "Sort By binder: grouped with count and value, within the binder by page and slot. Tap a binder's header for the page view.",
                "The page view shows each page as 3×3 with the cards in their real slots. The whole page always fits on one screen, without scrolling. Swipe or use the arrows. At the bottom is a strip of small pages; tap to jump. ▦ shows all pages at once.",
                "Foil = gold border with ✦, a stack = ×3. An empty slot has a dashed line: tap it to scan that one card right away, with binder, page and slot filled in.",
                "Tap a card for the card screen, hold it to move it. On the card screen, tapping the location takes you to that page with the slot highlighted.",
            )),
        )),
        Chapter("boosters", "Boosters", "Keeping track of what you paid and what came out.", listOf(
            Steps(listOf(
                "Scan the cards from your booster as usual. In the review screen tick This was a booster and fill in what you paid (the previous price is ready). You may pick the type (Play, Collector, Set).",
                "From a box? Tap From a box and fill in the count and price: the app works out the price per booster, and every next booster counts toward that box.",
                "After saving you see the result: paid, out of it, profit or loss, also without bulk, and the hit in large. Next booster sets everything up for the next one.",
                "Overview → Boosters shows per set and type how many you opened, what came out on average and what you paid. Per booster you see the value then and now.",
            )),
            Tip("Undoing the save also removes the booster. Remove a booster or change its price in Boosters; the cards stay in your collection."),
        )),
        Chapter("privacy", "Privacy mode", "Hiding amounts when someone else picks up your phone.", listOf(
            P("Tap the eye at the top of Collection, Decks or Overview. All amounts disappear, except in the trade match: total value, prices per card, the chart, Winner of the Week, the wishlist and boosters. Counts stay visible."),
            Steps(listOf(
                "Turning it on always works. Turning it off needs your fingerprint or your phone's screen lock.",
                "A quick look: hold the eye and confirm; you see the amounts for 15 seconds.",
                "While it is on, backup and CSV export (which contain prices) also ask for your fingerprint, and notifications show no amounts.",
                "Pick the style under Settings → View: Compleated (default), Seal, Shadow or Dots (calm). Changing the style also asks for your fingerprint.",
            )),
            Note("If your phone has no screen lock, the app cannot ask anything: the eye then works without confirmation."),
        )),
        Chapter("decks", "Decks", "Making decks, filling them from your collection and checking them.", listOf(
            H("A new deck"),
            Steps(listOf(
                "Go to Decks and tap New deck.",
                "Paste the decklist and tap Next.",
                "Name the deck and choose the format. The app suggests one (100 cards with a commander becomes Commander).",
                "Tap Save.",
            )),
            H("Putting cards from your collection into a deck"),
            P("A card is either in your collection or in a deck, never both. That way nothing is counted twice."),
            Steps(listOf(
                "Open the deck and tap From collection.",
                "Search by name or type. You only see cards you own that are not in a deck yet, with their location.",
                "Tap a card, choose the quantity and section (Commander, Deck or Sideboard) and tap Put in deck.",
            )),
            P("You can also work from a card: card screen → Move → choose the deck."),
            H("Pasting a list into a deck"),
            P("When you paste a list into a new or existing deck, the app checks each card against your collection. If you own it, Take from collection is on: the card moves out of your collection. Only what you don't own (enough of) is added as new. Bought an extra copy? Untick it."),
            P("If you own the card in a different print than the list says, you see in orange which print comes out of your collection (for example \"Other print from your collection: M10 146 ×2\"). Want the print from the list instead? Untick Take from collection. Basic lands are the exception: there the app only takes exactly the same print, so a list with particular lands gives you those lands."),
            Tip("The app takes the same print and finish first, then the same print, and only then another print of the same card. Proxies are never taken from your collection."),
            H("Cards back to your collection"),
            P("In the deck tap the card → Move → Collection. When deleting a whole deck you choose Keep cards (back to the collection) or Delete cards too."),
            H("Checks and bracket"),
            P("The top of the deck shows whether it is legal in its format: card count, sideboard, 4 or 1 copy limit, banned cards and commander colours. Commander decks get a bracket estimate based on the Game Changers list."),
            P("The app calls it at least bracket X and shows why: Game Changers, mass land denial, extra turns and tutors from the rules text."),
            Note("The bracket is an estimate. Combos only count once you have searched for them (Combos tab): also talk to your table."),
            H("Statistics"),
            P("The Decks tab groups your decks by format, with a heading. With the arrows you choose another order: value, name, number of cards or last changed; then it becomes one list. You can also search by name."),
            P("The Cards tab groups the cards by type (Creatures, Instants … Lands, with the sideboard separate), each with count and value. Tap a header to fold it open or shut; the app remembers this per deck. Sort within the groups by mana, name or price, and search with Search in deck. Each row shows the mana cost as on the card, and GC for a Game Changer. + Add offers From collection or Paste list."),
            P("At the top, a Commander deck shows a banner with the commander's art (with partners both names; tap a name for that card), and one line with format, number of cards, value, bracket and whether the deck is legal. Tap it for the details; with a problem it opens by itself. In the details, tap the format (with the pencil) to change it. A deck has four tabs: Cards, Statistics, Combos and Suggestions. Tap Statistics for four cards, each with an ⓘ: the mana curve with a verdict (does it fit aggro, midrange or control) and advice on the number of lands (Frank Karsten's formula); colours, with a bar for costs and one for lands per colour, and ⚠ when a colour lags behind (See lands takes you to the land suggestions); the opening hand, with the chance of 2 to 4 lands, the distribution and the Draw 7 button; and card types as one coloured bar."),
            P("Draw 7 shows a sample hand of seven random cards (without commander and sideboard). Mulligan shuffles again, Draw another takes the next card."),
            H("Suggestions"),
            Steps(listOf(
                "Open the Suggestions tab in a deck. The app looks in your collection for cards that fit: within the format, the deck's colours and your own rules.",
                "At the top you see which colours the app uses. With a commander these are its colours; otherwise a colour counts when at least 10% of your nonland cards have it, so one stray card does not widen the deck.",
                "Tap Rules for this deck: a creature type (for example Vampire), a highest bracket (Commander), Allow a splash (other formats: one extra colour your lands already make) and whether cards from other decks may be used.",
                "Per role (ramp, card draw, removal, board wipes …) you see a bar: green with ✓ when the target is met, orange when there are too few. Tap a role to see which cards count; with + Tick a card yourself you count a card the app does not recognise.",
                "The targets depend on the deck type. The app picks it (aggro with a tribe or many creatures, otherwise midrange), unless you choose aggro, midrange or control under Rules, or set your own target per role. The line Targets set for … shows what is used.",
                "At friends: loose cards from shared collections that would improve this deck, with your friend's name and the price. Tap to open the trade match.",
                "Tap a suggestion or Review swap. The swap window shows the card going in on the left and the card going out on the right. Pick another card or Nothing out, and the quantity (up to 4, Commander 1).",
                "For better lands you choose which basic land goes out, and which print. Basics in the new land's colours are at the top. Fetch lands count as the colours of the land types they search for.",
                "Tap a card under Could go out to choose what replaces it, or Nothing in.",
                "The blocks Could go in, Better lands and Could go out fold and unfold with a tap on the heading; the count is behind the title, with a short explanation below. The app remembers per deck what is open and closed.",
            )),
            Tip("A swap is one change: one undo reverts all of it. The card that goes out returns to your collection."),
            P("AI suggestions (when AI help is on): choose Only my collection or Also cards I do not have and tap Ask AI. Only card names and your deck rules are sent. Every suggestion is checked for colours, format and bracket; what does not fit is left out. Cards you do not own are listed under Consider buying, with price and link."),
            H("Combos"),
            Steps(listOf(
                "Open the Combos tab in a deck and tap Find combos. The app sends only the card names to Commander Spellbook, the large public combo database; you need internet.",
                "You see the combos in your deck with what they produce and what needs to be in place. Two-card combos are marked in red.",
                "Under Almost are combos that miss one card (dashed). If that card is in your collection, you see where and put it in the deck with In deck; if a friend has it, Trade match opens; if you don't have it, On wishlist adds it to your wishlist.",
                "For Commander, the card Influence on bracket shows how many two-card combos are in the deck.",
                "Two-card combos (as Commander Spellbook counts them) make the deck at least bracket 3. Spellbook does not reliably say whether such a combo comes early or late; its own estimate (for example Spicy or Ruthless) is shown next to it.",
                "If you change the deck after searching, the top says The deck changed – tap to search again. Until then only combos whose cards are all still in the deck count.",
            )),
            Tip("The result is kept until you change the deck; then search again."),
            H("Sharing and exporting"),
            P("The share icon sends the list to WhatsApp, mail or Moxfield. Via ⋮ → Export as text you save it as a file."),
        )),
        Chapter("overview", "Overview and prices", "What the numbers mean and where prices come from.", listOf(
            P("At the top is the Total value collection with the number of cards and the change since about a month ago. Below are Winner of the Week, the chart, the Value per rarity bar, one Sets line and the value per deck."),
            H("Winner of the Week"),
            P("Every Monday the app picks one card: the biggest rise of the past week, in money over the copies you own. Four copies rising €2 (€8) beat one rising €6. If nothing rose, the block is not shown."),
            H("Sets"),
            P("Tap Sets for all sets in a list. Sort by value, name, release date or count, or search by name or code. Per set you see the value, a rarity bar (tap it for the numbers) and how complete you are: how many of the regular card numbers you own, decks included. Turn on Completionist to count only your binders; a card that is only in a deck is then listed as missing, with the deck name."),
            H("The chart"),
            Steps(listOf(
                "Every day you open the app, and on every price update, the app keeps that day's numbers. So the chart fills up from the first day you use this version.",
                "Choose the period (1D, 1W, 1M, 3M, 1Y, All) and Value, Cards or Price movement. With 1D, 1W and 1M you also see moments within a day, such as a page you added in the afternoon (not for single sets); those are cleaned up after a month.",
                "Price movement moves only with prices: adding or removing cards does not count, so the jumps from new cards disappear. A card counts from the day you add it. A missed day is caught up later.",
                "The axis on the left does not start at zero but follows the lowest and highest value in the chosen period. That way even a change of a few euros shows. Tap or swipe across the chart for the exact amount of a day.",
                "With Value, the number of cards runs along as a second, thinner line, with its own axis on the right in the same colour. So you can see whether the value rises because you add cards or because they are worth more. The Number of cards button below the chart turns that line on or off.",
                "A dotted line means days without prices; the lighter part comes from your Sheet history.",
                "Choose lines: total collection, total sets, total decks, each deck and each set. At most 6 at a time. Tap a line in the legend to turn it off.",
                "Tap or swipe across the chart to see the values for a day.",
            )),
            Note("The line moves with price changes and with cards you add or remove. Look at Cards to see what caused a jump."),
            H("Price change"),
            P("Below the total value you see what the same cards are worth now compared to a week and a month ago. Cards you added or removed do not count: it is purely price movement. It appears a week after you install this version."),
            H("Prices in the background"),
            P("Every day the app updates prices on Wi-Fi, even if you do not open it; after 48 hours without Wi-Fi, over mobile data. Scryfall gives one price per print: language and condition do not count."),
            Tip("Breakout: when a card you own rises at least €3 and 25% in one day, you get a message, for example Breakout Creature. At most one a day; turn it off in Settings."),
            Steps(listOf(
                "Prices come from Scryfall: Cardmarket in euros or TCGplayer in dollars (choose in Settings).",
                "Usually the trend price, never the lowest price.",
                "Foils use the foil price. There is one price per print, regardless of language or condition.",
                "Tap the refresh icon at the top right to update all prices.",
            )),
            Note("Proxies count as zero. Cards are counted once: in your collection or in a deck."),
        )),
        Chapter("share", "Share and trade", "Send your collection, view friends' collections and see what you can trade.", listOf(
            P("Under More → Share and trade. You send a small file (usually 30 to 100 KB) by WhatsApp, e-mail or anything else. Only cards and quantities go along, with foil and language. No prices: the receiver's app looks them up at Scryfall itself, so you always see the same, current prices. Proxies are left out."),
            H("Sharing your collection"),
            Steps(listOf(
                "Tap Choose and share.",
                "The first time you enter the name you share under, for example Mick. The app remembers it; you can change it every time. The file is then called NineGrid - Mick.ninegrid.",
                "Choose what to send: Everything (your loose collection and all decks), only the loose collection, or individual binders, sets and decks. Combining is fine.",
                "At the bottom you see how many cards in how many parts. Tap Share and choose the app to send with, or Save as file.",
            )),
            Tip("Send your decks along, and your friend can also see which of your cards improve their decks, and the other way round."),
            P("Sending again with the same choice replaces the old version at your friend's. Every sender has a fixed code, so this works even if you change your name. Send something else (for example only one deck) and it is added next to it."),
            H("Receiving a collection"),
            Steps(listOf(
                "Tap the file in WhatsApp or Files and choose NineGrid, or tap Open file in Share and trade.",
                "The collection appears under Collections of others, per person. Below it are the parts you received: Loose collection, Binder Red, Deck Edgar …",
                "View only: it never mixes with your own collection, does not count in your value and you cannot change it.",
            )),
            P("Someone without NineGrid? An export from Moxfield, ManaBox, Archidekt, Deckbox, Dragon Shield, TCGplayer, Delver Lens or Helvault also opens with Open file. The app asks whose collection it is and adds it like a shared one."),
            P("You can keep as many people as you like. The pencil gives someone another name (only on your phone). The bin removes the person; remove a single part by selecting it and tapping the bin in its label."),
            H("Trade match"),
            Steps(listOf(
                "Open a person and choose the Trade match tab.",
                "From <name>, for your decks: their loose cards that improve one of your decks, with the same logic as the deck suggestions (colours, format, bracket and your deck rules). Each card says for which decks and why.",
                "From you, for the decks of <name>: your loose cards that improve their decks. This only works if they sent decks along.",
                "Tick what you want to trade. At the bottom you see what you get and what you give, in your own currency, and whether it is about even.",
            )),
            P("You see trades without looking for them: Overview has a Trade block with, per friend, how many cards for your decks they have (tap = straight to the trade match), a deck's Suggestions tab shows At friends, and the card screen says Also at: Jan ×2. Send your wishlist along and the top of the trade match shows what the other has from your wishlist, and the other way round."),
            Note("The trade match works with loose cards. Cards that are in one of their decks are not suggested."),
        )),
        Chapter("undo", "Going back (change log)", "What is kept and how to undo something.", listOf(
            P("Every change goes into the change log: adding, moving, editing and deleting cards, and creating, changing or deleting decks."),
            Steps(listOf(
                "Go to More → Change log.",
                "Tap Undo latest change.",
                "Another step back? Tap again. Undone lines are struck through.",
            )),
            Tip("A whole deck saved in one go is one change too. One tap reverts everything, including the cards that came from your collection."),
            Note("Cannot be undone: settings, price updates and restoring a backup. So make a backup before restoring one."),
        )),
        Chapter("backup", "Backup and new phone", "Keeping your data safe and taking it with you.", listOf(
            P("Everything lives on this phone. If it breaks or you get a new one, you need a backup."),
            Steps(listOf(
                "Go to More → Settings and backup → Backup and export.",
                "Back up now: choose a place, for example Google Drive or Downloads.",
                "Weekly automatic backup: turn it on and choose a folder. The app puts a new file there every week.",
                "On a new phone: install NineGrid, tap Restore and choose the backup file.",
            )),
            P("The backup holds everything that is yours: cards and decks with their rules, the history, wishlist and price alerts, boosters, friends with their shared collections, your own share code (so friends recognise you after restoring), the change log and your settings. Not included: the AI key (it stays on this phone only), the offline card database and the images; you download those again."),
            P("After making one you see what is in it, for example \"1,069 cards · 6 decks · 1,243 price points · 3 friends · settings\". You see the same line before restoring, with the date of the backup."),
            Note("When restoring you choose what to restore: everything by default, or separate parts (only the decks, or everything except the settings). What you choose replaces what is on the phone; what you leave out stays as it is. An older backup holds less; what is not in it also stays. If you restore only the collection or only the decks, the change log is emptied."),
            P("After your first 20 cards the app asks once for a backup folder. Your collection is also part of the normal Android backup of your phone, so a new phone gets it back."),
            H("Erase everything"),
            P("Under Settings → Erase everything (in red, on its own) you choose what to erase: collection, decks, history, change log and images. A backup is made first, and you confirm by typing ERASE. If you keep the change log, one tap undoes it."),
            H("Exporting"),
            P("Export collection (CSV) creates a file you can open in Google Sheets or Excel."),
        )),
        Chapter("settings", "Settings", "Eight groups, each showing how it is set now.", listOf(
            P("More → Settings and backup opens an overview with eight groups. Under each group one line shows how it is set now; tap it to open it. Back returns to the overview. The ? at the top right opens the chapter for that group."),
            H("1. Display"),
            P("Theme (day, night or follow phone), language, currency (EUR via Cardmarket or USD via TCGplayer) and date and time: 24 or 12 hours, the order of the date, which day the week starts (also for Winner of the Week) and whether the weekday is shown. Only the display changes: saving, exports and backups always use 2026-11-05."),
            P("Pick day or night with the sun and the moon. Guild colour puts buttons and charts in a mana colour or a pair of two (the logo stays the same). Magic effects turns the foil shine, the exile animation and the stamps on or off. Privacy mode and its style are here too (see the chapter Privacy mode)."),
            H("2. Scanning"),
            P("Automatic capture for single cards and how fast, vibration, shutter sound, and whether recognition times are shown under the result (off by default)."),
            H("3. Card data"),
            P("Store images (off, small or full; only for cards you own) and Wi-Fi only. The offline card database: off, on new set or manual only. On means scanning without internet and fast imports, but one large download and space on your phone. Prices still come from the daily update. Download via Wi-Fi only, or also mobile data (with a question first, and automatically only if you turn that on separately)."),
            H("4. Collection"),
            P("Completionist: when on, set completeness only counts cards in your binders, not in decks. Breakout alerts: a message when a card you own rises at least €3 and 25% in a day. Bulk limit for boosters: cards below this amount (€0.25 by default) don't count in the result without bulk."),
            H("5. AI help"),
            P("Off by default. Choose a service (Gemini has a free tier, Claude, OpenAI, DeepSeek, Mistral, OpenRouter, Groq or your own address), paste your key and tap Test. When scanning, the AI only reads orange or not-found slots; the app checks the result at Scryfall. With a daily maximum. The key is stored encrypted on this phone and is not in the backup."),
            P("When the service is busy (overloaded or too many requests), the app quietly tries again after 2, 5 and 10 seconds; that counts as one request. If it still fails, you get one message saying what is going on: service overloaded (not your key), service limit reached, key not accepted, unknown model or no connection. Test retries only once, so you get an answer quickly."),
            Tip("Test says Gemini is overloaded? Try later, fill in another model (for example a lite variant from Google AI Studio), or choose another service."),
            H("6. Backup and export"),
            P("Back up now, restore, the weekly automatic backup and the collection as CSV. See the chapter Backup and new phone."),
            H("7. Erase everything"),
            P("On its own and in red. You choose what to erase; a backup always comes first."),
            H("8. About NineGrid"),
            P("Version and planeswalker, check for updates, What's new (the window you see after an update), the guide and the credits."),
            P("Updating happens from the app: once a day it checks for a new version and downloads it (by default only on wifi; also mobile or off is chosen here). You get a notification; tap Update and confirm in the Android window. The first time, Android asks once to allow installing apps from this source. From Android 12 on it often works without a tap after that."),
        )),
        Chapter("help", "Troubleshooting", "When something doesn't do what you expect.", listOf(
            H("The scanner doesn't recognise cards"),
            Steps(listOf(
                "Enter the set of the page; then only the number or name has to be read.",
                "More light, no glare, phone straight above the page.",
                "Make sure the page fills the frame and isn't crooked.",
                "Anything not found can be picked yourself in the review screen with the magnifier.",
            )),
            H("No image for a card"),
            P("Check that you have internet (or Wi-Fi, if Only on Wi-Fi is on). Lists show no images when Store images is Off. If it still fails, the reason is shown where the image should be."),
            H("Cardmarket blocks"),
            P("The Cardmarket button opens the search page for the card name. If Cardmarket keeps blocking, open the link in another browser or try again later."),
            H("Installing an update"),
            P("When you see Update available, tap Download and open the file. The new version installs over the old one; your cards and decks stay."),
        )),
    )
}
